        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: наезд",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "наезд (nayézd) — \"a hit (by a vehicle)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Вчера на углу был наезд на мальчика. Vcherá na uglú byl nayézd na málchika. Yesterday a boy was hit by a car on the corner."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Наезд на + accusative."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "наезд (nayézd) is built on наехать \"to run into\", from на- and ехать \"to go by vehicle\", inherited from Proto-Slavic ěxati \"to travel\" (EtymDB)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
